' =============================================================================
' The render tick, proposed
' =============================================================================
note as TICK #E8F5E9
  **Engine::update(dt) - two-pass**
  1. now = clock.now(); advance TimeContext
  2. **short-circuit**: if no layer changed() and now < min(nextDue),
     skip to 6 - the master frame and every DMX buffer are already correct
  3. **render**: each layer composes its OWN frame
       stack.compose() -> per effect: due() ? evaluate() : cached, then replay
       a stack whose effects were all cached returns its cached frame untouched
  4. **fold**: Compositor merges layer frames low -> high into the master frame,
     per category, using each layer's MergeConfig; PresetRefs resolved here
  5. **resolve**: Renderer merge-walks master frame x fid index ->
     Fixture::Resolve() -> Cell::Resolve() -> Parameter::Write() -> buffer
  6. **output**: OutputStage sends dirty universes + keepalive via IDmxSink
  7. nextWake = min(nextDue) across all effects -> the loop sleeps on a timer,
     not on a fixed 25 ms
end note
TICK .. Engine

note as FOLD #E3F2FD
  **Why the fold rule is what it is**
  LTP per category: the highest-priority layer holding a value wins outright -
  grab a fixture on the programmer and it overrides a running cue; release it
  and the cue shows through, untouched, because the cue never lost its value.
  HTP per category: find the highest priority TIER with any value, take the max
  WITHIN that tier, ignore lower tiers. Priority beats HTP - that is what makes
  "park this playback above the programmer" mean something, and it is the
  behaviour MA and ChamSys operators already have in their hands.
end note
FOLD .. Compositor

note as DEP #F3E5F5
  **The dependency rule**
  Definition -> Fixture -> Patch -> Frame/Layers/Effects -> Show -> Engine.
  Arrows point one way. The core names no socket, no file, no parser: it
  declares IDmxSink, IClock, IFixtureLibrary, IShowStore and someone else
  implements them. Make it a link-time rule, not a convention: a core CMake
  target that links neither Utils::Network nor synparser cannot regress.
  The payoff is not purity - it is that RecordingSink + ManualClock let you
  assert "chase at 120 BPM, frame 37, fixture 12 = 0.71" in a unit test.
end note

note as ORDER #FFF8E1
  **A sane order to get there**
  1. Selection (+ Interval revision) - deletes FixtureGroup, FixtureSelection,
     StaticEffectHolder and fixes stale caches in one move.
  2. Patch reindex invariant + repatch() - D1 and D6, small and self-contained.
  3. EffectId / EffectHandle / EffectStack - unblocks editing a running effect.
  4. EffectSpec + EffectFactory (port from old/) - unblocks store and recall,
     and therefore Preset<Cat>, Cue and Sequence.
  5. Layer::render() + MergeConfig + Compositor - the one genuinely invasive
     change; do it after 3 so the programmer already renders from stacks.
  6. Ports + adapters, then RenderLoop short-circuit.
  7. Attribute enum + Classifier + GDTF import - large, but purely additive
     once FixtureValues is category-sloted.
end note

@enduml
